<!-- From -->
Gaffer had these answers to the questions in italics on the <a class=post href=http://boards.xrgaming.com/cgi/origin/devboard.cgi?view>CoNB DevBoard</a>:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
<I>4) Lack of variety. Variety is the spice of life. At least AC had this part right. They are able to add new dungeons constantly. Currently, their's over 100 dungeons I believe. Some for solo'ers, some for groups, some for newbies, some for powerlevelers, etc. </I><br>
</quote><p>
We have the same capability to add new dungeons after ship.  Dunno how many we'll ship with (not dodging that question, I would just need to go ask our worldbuilders and find out what they have scheduled) but we can add arbitrary amounts after ship, and cheaply from a patch size standpoint.  So no fears, if we ship with too few, we can add more.  We'd rather not ship with too few of course.<p>
<quote><I>I REALLY hope they add more dungeons to UO2. I hated that I could never really go throught the dungeons in UO. Either the dungeons were infested with PK's, or they were filled with monsters that one-hit you (Not good in any game). </I><br>
</quote><p>
Some dungeons are in NPK lands.  Some dungeons are gonna be very tough.  Some will be easier.  There are also lots of non-dungeon areas in which to kill monsters as well...including areas in buildings, etc. which aren't "Dungeons" <I>per se</I> but aren't purely outdoors.
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


