<!-- From -->
Mobius had this comment on the <a class=post href=http://boards.xrgaming.com/cgi/origin/devboard.cgi?view>CoNB DevBoard</a> concerning skills and the usefullness of certain ones:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
While we've got enough spiffy features in each of the skill trees to make them worthwhile, not all will be equal in power and prestige. I do not think that this is necessarily a bad thing. Certain skill sets such as magic and combat, by their nature, are more powerful than a skill tree like cooking. Fortunately, we are able to use skill costs in order to balance this out. Since combat is a more powerful skill tree than cooking, it is much more costly to learn. 
<p>
That isn't to say cooking is useless. We've provided enough in game benefits to chefs to make them valuable.
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


