<!-- From -->
ImaFreak had some questions about our <a class=post href=http://uo2vault.ign.com/guidebook/skill_trees/default.asp>Skills and Skill Trees</a> guide and Ubiq gave these answers to his questions (in italics) on the UWOO@egroups.com mailing list:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
<i> Hi, first off, great job on the whole thing, very detailed, 
 even I, a sucker
 of knowledge, learned a few things(well, I hadn't known they 
 were confirmed
 atleast :P).
 I am wondering, will axes be completely smithed by 
 Blacksmiths? If so, will
 the shafts be metal? If there was a way to balance it out, it 
 would be nice
 so that axes took wooden shafts, thus making even trade skill 
 people unite
 amongst each other :)</i>
<p>
For some crafting skills this is the case, but for others, less
so.  The key is to find a good balance between cooperation and
preventing total annoyance.
<p>
<i> A second thought, there were a few things I was wondering about:
 "What Is a Skill Box"-I have never seen a dev comment on the 
 fact that you
 cant put multiple ankhs into 1 skill box, though I guess it is assumed
 pretty well :)</i>
<p>
You can't put more ankhs in a box than it costs.  A skill box is 
binary, meaning you either have it or you don't.  In the example
tree, once you spend 2 ankhs to get Simple Metalworks, you have it
and any future ankhs should be spend on the boxes that it 'unlocks'.
<p>
<i> Was the "How do stats Improve" mentioned as for sure yet?</i>
<p>
This has been decided for sure.
<p>
<i> I remember them saying they would keep the 3 main stats for 
 Origin, but did
 they ever say they wont have sub-stats? Like coordination, 
 etc. Maybe these
 will just be skills.</i>
<p>
Yes, there will be 'substats' but most of them will be largely 
invisible to the players.
<p>
<i> I also havent heard on Titles :)
 Well, I will stop now, probably going to confuse myself, hehe.
 Just wondering if any of this was implied and not official, no biggie.
 Thanks for the great info!(The skills tree's were awesome)</i>
<p>
Titles are associated with a skill box.  For example, front kick will 
deliver with it the 'Kick Boxer' title.  As you move further into the
tree, your title will be improved ('Journeyman Kick Boxer', 'Advanced
Kick Boxer', etc.)
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


