			<font face="Arial" size="-1" color="Black">
<!-- From -->
Audball had this to say on our <a class=post href=http://vnboards.ign.com/board.asp?brd=5166>DevBoard</a> concerning 3D audio:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
Ubiq is indeed correct in stating that ORIGIN does have full 3D sound.  Basically, I took the Ascension sound system and improved it in 3 main ways:
<br>
<br>1) It's now multi-threaded, so you shouldn't get any of those annoying pauses or repeats in audio that you sometimes would in Ascension.  (Remember Hawkind saying &quot;Arise, Avatar... atar... atar...&quot;? ;-)
<br>
<br>2) A better priority system is used, so you should get fewer sounds getting cut off for others in many cases.
<br>
<br>3) We're using a different (better, IMO) format of music, giving us much better control over what plays when, and in a more interactive manner (eg. we could pump up the tempo or add a mood overlay when your health gets critically low in combat, etc.)
<br>
<br>If you want to know specific technologies/APIs we're using for sound, here's the list:  DirectSound, DirectSound3D, DirectMusic.  (Basically, everthing DirectX gives us :-)
<br>
<br>As for A3D, EAX, or other additional APIs we could use for audio effects, we haven't decided what, if any, we'll support on ship.  I personally would prefer to stick to the DirectX route and use IA3DL2 (basically EAX 2.5 was integrated into DirectX 8 as Microsoft's  standard for acoustics/reverberation).  Adding it shouldn't be too difficult since we have the Ascension code to work with, but we haven't found the right place for it on the schedule yet.  My guess is that'd it would be deemed a post-ship feature/improvement.  (I'd personally agree with Ubiq and vote for things like housing to get done first.)
<br>
<br>Cheers,
<br>Audball
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


