<!-- From -->
Austen Andrews had the following to say on the UWOO@egroups.com mailing list in reply to the comments in italics:
<!-- End From -->
<!-- Begin Story -->
<!-- Indent --><table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0"><tr><td width="15"><img src="/images/blank.gif" width=15 height=1 border=0 alt=""></td><td><font face="Arial" size="-1" color="#000068"><!-- End Indent-->
<i> I would like to personally thank Ahriman and Austin Andrews on how they ended the fiction in a great way. Something I haven't seen many stories have that makes them great.</i>
<p>
You're very much welcome.  Personally I'll echo the thanks to Ahriman
for being a great editor and coming up with such wonderful plots to hang
my purple prose on.  For those of you who don't know him, Ahriman is an
amazing guy, easily the most extraordinary person I know.  He has an
unbelievable talent for characters and storylines.  His instinct for
what's cool and what's not is dead on (and he's not afraid to tell you
when you cross that line!).  EA is damn lucky to have someone with his
abilities on their payroll.  I feel certain the dev team will back me up
on that.
<p>
He's also notorious for abusing the Hell out of his characters, as
anyone who's read the final Britannia chapter has seen.  It ended like a
Shakespearean tragedy, didn't it?  What gloriously dark fun for a writer
to flesh out.
<p>
<i> I was wondering a few things, first, does this mean you will not produce any more things with Lord British in them?</i>
<p>
I'm just a contractor, so I'll leave it to Ahriman or someone else from
EA to elaborate, if they so choose.  Though I thought he was pretty
clear in his letter.
<p>
<i> I also wonder, are your new books, the ones published by PocketBooks, going to be about Ultima Origin?</i>
<p>
Yes.  I can't say anything more, except to point out that Ahriman
mentioned the books in his letter from May 19th.  And that we're wildly
working to produce a trilogy that will far outpace the standards we've
set in the prequel fiction.
<p>
<i> Thanks again :)</i>
<p>
It's been my pleasure.  :)
<!-- /Indent --></font></td></tr></table><!-- End /Indent -->
<!-- End Story -->
<!-- Thanks -->
Thanks!
<!-- End Thanks -->
</font>


